.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_CONFIG
the config folder (default ~/.config/deploys)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_DIR
where providers/ (and, without one next to the script, lib/) are
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_READONLY
observer mode: any value but 0, false, no, off turns it on
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_NO_GITHUB
ask no git host (as status \-\-no\-github)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_JOURNAL
the deploy journal file (default: the app's, on Linux in the config folder)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_NOTIFY
0: no macOS notifications from autofix and guard
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_TEAM_TTL
seconds a shared deploy\-center.json is cached (default 600)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_AUTOFIX_PER_DAY, DEPLOYS_AUTOFIX_PER_PROJECT
autofix caps per 24 h (default 6 and 2)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_GITLAB_HOSTS
self\-managed GitLab hosts (docs/GITLAB.md)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_HTTP_TRACE
1: one line per call to a platform on stderr (method, path without query, status, time; no header, no body); \-\-debug sets it
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_QUIET, DEPLOYS_DEBUG
what the global \-\-quiet and \-\-debug set: only the result; the trace of the calls
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_PARALLEL
how many platform or git host reads run at once in a list (default 8, at most 32; 3 while GitHub's budget is under 1000)
.TP
.B HTTP_DEADLINE
seconds one platform call may take in all, tries and waits included (default 120)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_CLOUDFLARE_PER_PAGE
page size of the Cloudflare project list (default 10)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
the key for deploys ai, before ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and the keychain
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_ANTHROPIC_API
the base address of the Anthropic API for deploys ai (default https://api.anthropic.com/v1); it must be https, because it receives your key
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_VERCEL_USD_PER_MIN, DEPLOYS_RENDER_USD_PER_MIN
build\-minute prices for simulate and ledger
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_TIMEOUT
the older name of DEPLOYS_CLI_TIMEOUT, used where that is not set
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_LOG_MAX_BYTES
size past which a job log is renamed to .1 (default 1 MB); runs from launchd rotate by themselves, others with DEPLOYS_LOG_ROTATE=1
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_CLI_TIMEOUT
seconds a gh api, glab api or vercel api call may take (default 90; 0 no limit). The Vercel CLI asks DEPLOYS_VERCEL_TIMEOUT first (default 60), then this one
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_VERCEL_TIMEOUT
seconds one vercel call may take (default 60; falls back to DEPLOYS_CLI_TIMEOUT when that is set)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_VERCEL_TEAM
the Vercel team id, if the token sees several teams
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_AMPLIFY_PROFILE
the aws CLI profile for Amplify
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_CLOUDFLARE_TOGGLE
1: Cloudflare deploys switch push\-builds on for the start (providers/cloudflare.md)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_COOLIFY_ALLOW_HTTP
1: the Coolify token may go to a plain http:// instance that is not this machine
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_NETLIFY_POLLS
how often a Netlify start looks for its new build (default 15)
.TP
.B <NAME>_CMD
a command that prints a key, asked after the variable <NAME> and before the keychain (RENDER_API_KEY_CMD='op read op://vault/render/key'; 1Password, pass, Vault, a company tool). First line of its output, 20 s limit. For CI and for Macs where the keychain is off limits
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_NOTIFY_CMD
your own command for notifications (ntfy, a webhook through curl, notify\-send on Linux): the text is on its stdin and in DEPLOYS_MESSAGE, 20 s limit
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_CI_GRACE
seconds a young commit without any check counts as "CI not started yet" for \-\-when\-green (default 90; SAFE\-DEPLOY.md)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_CI_IGNORE
a regex for check names that do not count for \-\-when\-green (an optional check that is always red)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_NO_JOURNAL
1: a start from the terminal writes no journal line (tests, containers)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_CALLER
app: set by the Mac app when it runs deploys; the terminal journal line is skipped because the app writes its own (do not set it in scripts: you would lose the journal entry)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_LIB
1: source deploys only loads the functions and runs nothing (what providers/hook.sh and the tests do)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_HOOK_TIMEOUT
seconds one hooks.d script may run (default 300; 0 no limit; see "Hooks" below)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_LOG_ROTATE
1: rotate the job log of this run (the jobs from schedule, guard schedule and autofix schedule set it; DEPLOYS_LOG_MAX_BYTES is the size)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_FOLLOW_EVERY
seconds between two reads of logs \-\-follow (default 5)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_STRIP_ESC
1: cut colors and control characters out of build logs also on a pipe or into a file (for text that goes into a ticket)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_ROUTINE_API
where autofix hand\-overs go (default Anthropic's routines API; https only, it receives your token)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_ROUTINE_BETA
the anthropic\-beta header of those calls (default experimental\-cc\-routine\-2026\-04\-01); set it when Anthropic renames the beta and autofix answers with an API error (AUTOFIX.md)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_SCAN_FOREGROUND
1: scan start and check start run in the foreground instead of a background process, so a CI job ends after the scan (SCAN.md)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_TEAM_REFRESH
1: read the shared files from GitHub again whatever the cache's age (as team refresh; the age is DEPLOYS_TEAM_TTL)
.TP
.B DEPLOYS_LAUNCH_DIR
another folder for the launchd job files (default ~/Library/LaunchAgents; for tests and sandboxed accounts)
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
no color
.TP
.B \-\-color=always, \-\-color=never, \-\-color=auto, \-\-no\-color
on the command line, anywhere; the last one wins and beats NO_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE (auto clears both: a terminal gets color, a pipe does not)
